{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes","id":582155,"title":"[Beast] Changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T04:54:02-07:00","id":582155,"title":"[Beast] Changes","content":"Anyone got a summary over there of what the revisions entailed? Was the KS document updated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:05:05-07:00","id":582294,"title":"","content":"They added the Beast cultural perspective of &quot;teaching mortals through the primal fears they've used civilization to insulate themselves against&quot;; the term Homecoming was replaced by Devouring - with the idea that in most cases other Beasts are involved in devouring your vestigial mortal soul to allow your true nature to take hold (thus reinforcing a familial bond at entrance into ones existence as one of the Begotten), it is now an open question of the setting whether the Begotten are purely transformed by the Devouring or realizing their true nature that has always been; the Ugallu and Namtaru Birthrights were fixed; anyone else want to keep going?<br /> <br /> Here's the most current drafts we've seen: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/a/solutions-edu.com/folderview?id=0B66tiMNn-_PVflpVYlNrQWJXcjRKekdFRmpRdF9ybU5WRzRIc2JmOGdUdUwyaE1SeVBSaFU&amp;usp=sharing#\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/a/solutions...U&amp;usp=sharing#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:25:29-07:00","id":582343,"title":"","content":"Heroes now come in different categories including ones that actually want to help people and aren't complete psychos. It is just acknowledged that a Hero with no interest in combating or opposing the Beast in anyway makes a poor antagonist and won't be getting much more word count than saying they exist.<br /> Heroes are now kind of like Beasts in that they're always more connected to the Primordial Dream than most people and Beasts now sort of awaken them as opposed to creating them. <br /> Becoming an Apex Beast now has more methods to do so than just completely no sell a Hero who comes to destroy you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:29:42-07:00","id":582361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=582294#post582294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They added the Beast cultural perspective of &quot;teaching mortals through the primal fears they've used civilization to insulate themselves against&quot;; the term Homecoming was replaced by Devouring - with the idea that in most cases other Beasts are involved in devouring your vestigial mortal soul to allow your true nature to take hold (thus reinforcing a familial bond at entrance into ones existence as one of the Begotten), it is now an open question of the setting whether the Begotten are purely transformed by the Devouring or realizing their true nature that has always been; (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The bit about the Devouring was since changed again. The intro has just not been updated to reflect that. Nascent Beasts are still presented as having an inherent connection to the Primordial Dream and their Horror, heavily spoken of as their true soul whether they accept it or not; and having the process of becoming a Beast <i>facilitated</i> by the involvement of another Beast in the Devouring is spoken of with the same validity as those that happen on their own, so neither is necessarily more to norm than the other.<br /> <br /> Heroes also got some significant tweaks that give them a bigger place in the Beast cosmology and a stronger connection to the Primordial Dream. They are, however, not necessarily created by Beasts anymore so much as they are spurred to action and awakened to their own nature by the ripples Begotten create in the Primordial Dream. There are also &quot;good&quot; Heroes and their existence is discussed in perspective of the kind of people the Heroes Beasts tend to meet really are, even if they don't actually feature in the game.<br /> <br /> And the Primordial Dream was expanded upon with, among other things, its supposed ancient significance to the survival of humanity that contributes to the cultural perspective of Beasts to &quot;teach through fear&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some of the examples of Beasts in the book were deliberately softened, and as Nalak mentioned the Incarnates were expanded in regards to the methods by which they can achive the Inheritance, as well as being given a very interesting vulnerability in the form of reliance on the stability of their Myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:29:01-07:00","id":582625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=582361#post582361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the examples of Beasts in the book were deliberately softened</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my least favorite tweak (a lot of the changes I ADORE). It's just so unnecessary. Yes, there should be diversity in the moral presentation of the Beasts, but in a game about monsters there shouldn't be a reason to shy away from the negative end of the spectrum. I mean - just look at Vampire!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:36:17-07:00","id":582722,"title":"","content":"That one suprised me. I was watching the RPG.net threads and people weren't asking for Beasts to be softened, they just wanted the book to acknowledge what Beasts were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T05:54:46-07:00","id":583414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=582722#post582722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one suprised me. I was watching the RPG.net threads and people weren't asking for Beasts to be softened, they just wanted the book to acknowledge what Beasts were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall anyone asking for Beasts to be softened, no, but I do recall seeing people say they couldn't play Beasts as they were or appeared to be in the first draft.<br /> <br /> I'd have preferred more examples rather than softened ones, but if the latter gets more people to revisit the game than the former, then I'll take it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T06:20:19-07:00","id":583426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583414#post583414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall anyone asking for Beasts to be softened, no, but I do recall seeing people say they couldn't play Beasts as they were or appeared to be in the first draft.<br /> <br /> I'd have preferred more examples rather than softened ones, but if the latter gets more people to revisit the game than the former, then I'll take it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That'd be my preference as well, but in splat pages, I'm limited by space, so I went with the option of softening some of the characters so we didn't have <i>quite</i> so many serial killers in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:15:47-07:00","id":583480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583426#post583426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd be my preference as well, but in splat pages, I'm limited by space, so I went with the option of softening some of the characters so we didn't have <i>quite</i> so many serial killers in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely fair. Though given the tone of a lot of the criticism, I'd probably have taken &quot;Fuck the lot of you, no more Onyx Path stuff ever&quot; as pretty fair. (Edit: thinking of RPGNet more than here with that last part).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:18:14-07:00","id":583527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=582294#post582294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They added the Beast cultural perspective of &quot;teaching mortals through the primal fears they've used civilization to insulate themselves against&quot;;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to admit something here, I was really interested in Beast until this came about. I have no problem with Beasts having something to do, but it makes Beasts into jerks (oh, you're a beast, here, go and scare the mortals into remembering what they are) and it's not really something I can base a lot of campaigns around. Although the only example I've been able to come up with for something else for them to do has them basically assembling time capsules, so all this has done is convince me to pick it up later, rather than back the kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:16:46-07:00","id":583565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583527#post583527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with Beasts having something to do, but it makes Beasts into jerks (oh, you're a beast, here, go and scare the mortals into remembering what they are)</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be a bit more benign than that. A beast could work like the Scarecrow Ministry, creating an obviously frightening aura around a place so that people don't go there and get eaten by the more subtle but malign thing that lives there. Or a Beast with the Hunger for Hoard or Ruin could be a Buddhist of sorts, evangelising the impermanence of material things. A Charmer slasher might suddenly find that everyone inexplicably gets the creeps round him, making it harder to find people to kill (I'm assuming the Beast has some reason not to just kill him or get him caught). Preventative measures against things are driven in part by the fear of those things, so a few nightmares about falling might impel the city council to finally get round to fixing that busted railing on the bridge. In controlled circumstances, fear can be cathartic, so a Beast might engage in really scary performance art. That lawyer in the example Beasts is teaching the connected that there <i>are</i> those who will stand up for their victims.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the game says that some Beasts eschew the teaching angle to just revel - by extension, some could also eschew the teaching angle because they don't really buy into it, but still try to live harmlessly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:29:48-07:00","id":583578,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't buy the whole Wisdom schtick. The way I'm planning to pitch it to my players is... &quot;You're a Beast, you prey on and assert your dominance over humans through nightmares. They've forgotten their place in the world and you Hunger to remind them why they should fear the dark.&quot; -- a bit less preachy on the whole school marm vibe the current draft has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:31:39-07:00","id":583580,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'd like my players to have a chance to play it a little more like Smaug and a little less &quot;You kids better knock it off or, I'm going to pull this car over.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast's should have enormous egos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:32:37-07:00","id":583676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583578#post583578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't buy the whole Wisdom schtick. The way I'm planning to pitch it to my players is... &quot;You're a Beast, you prey on and assert your dominance over humans through nightmares. They've forgotten their place in the world and you Hunger to remind them why they should fear the dark.&quot; -- a bit less preachy on the whole school marm vibe the current draft has.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is completely consistent with how it's written, it's just that there are a lot of other perspectives within Beast society. The perspective you're expressing is still &quot;teaching&quot; in Beast POV, it's just that the lesson in question is &quot;COWER BEFORE THE EMBODIMENTS OF YOUR FEAR&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:41:27-07:00","id":583682,"title":"","content":"I don't think many people forgot that. Vampire comparisons were thick and fast over at RPG.net","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:41:45-07:00","id":583684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone remembers White Wolf's original flagship gameline was and is about walking talking rape-metaphors, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be careful with comparing the two: It spawned a massive argument over in RPG.net. I'm not trying to suggest that would happen here, but apparently it's not as iron-clad a comparison as you'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:45:07-07:00","id":583693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583682#post583682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think many people forgot that. Vampire comparisons were thick and fast over at RPG.net</div> </div> </div> </div>Which should only be a problem if the game isn't presenting them as being monsters.<br /> <br /> But as I've said before, far too many address the WoD (both of them) as superhero settings, and treat mechanics meant to reinforce themes as though they're there for balance (I lost count of the number of people I've seen claim that Classic Vampire &quot;Humanity&quot; was meant to make you act moral; which is the opposite of the truth, it's there to reflect the character's downward spirals and struggle with their morality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:48:38-07:00","id":583698,"title":"","content":"Rpg.net is <i>batshit insane</i>.<br /> <br /> We should be fine here. I think. Maybe.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change the fact that there's a lot of obvious allegory going on, although a large part of the is the fault of popular vampire media and Stoker's hangups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:51:18-07:00","id":583701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583693#post583693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which should only be a problem if the game isn't presenting them as being monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it backwards. The comparisons were saying that Vampire's presentation was the correct way to sensitively handle monstrous protagonists like Beasts.<br /> <br /> The RPG.net threads are extremely long and start going around in circles after a while, but there's a lot of respected long time posters in there. It's worth giving them a read; if only to understand other people's points of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583693#post583693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen claim that Classic Vampire &quot;Humanity&quot; was meant to make you act moral; which is the opposite of the truth, it's there to reflect the character's downward spirals and struggle with their morality).</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with that complaint though.<br /> <br /> You're right that it misunderstands the authorial intent. But on the other hand I'm a strong believer in mechanics that reward players for acting in theme. Thus, since vampires are supposed to loose Humanity lower Humanity should be mechanically advantageous over high Humanity. Or even better; it should have advantages and disadvantages - carefully constructed so that the only charachter who benefits from high Humanity is one who wants to be moral. Everyone else, who wishes to succeed in the Danse, is better of with low Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-08-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:04:09-07:00","id":583711,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, criticizing how well it succeeds at it's goal is one thing - but my point was people so often approach Humanity, Paradox, etc as though they only exist with the goal of balancing mechanical advantages, and completely ignore the thematic intent. I'm all for the NWoD Second Edition adjustments using Conditions/Beats as a carrot to reinforce said themes rather than a stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:30:35-07:00","id":583744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583698#post583698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rpg.net is <i>batshit insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sometimes get the insanity vibe; but I agreed with the general thrust of the criticisms anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583698#post583698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't change the fact that there's a lot of obvious allegory going on, although a large part of the is the fault of popular vampire media and Stoker's hangups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. You talking about Beast or Vampire here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583711#post583711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, criticizing how well it succeeds at it's goal is one thing - but my point was people so often approach Humanity, Paradox, etc as though they only exist with the goal of balancing mechanical advantages, and completely ignore the thematic intent. I'm all for the NWoD Second Edition adjustments using Conditions/Beats as a carrot to reinforce said themes rather than a stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're doing that they're wrong. I believe balance is important* but not that Humanity or Paradox are primarally there for balance.<br /> <br /> * In a slightly odd way. To use my own work as an example, I try very hard to make sure that Princesses with ranged weapons were balanced against Princesses with melee weapons because magical girl shows portray both as equal. On the other hand if a Princesses are consistently gaining more combat power for their exp than Demons I wouldn't mind; because most magical girls are warriors and Demons are spies. On the other hand if Princesses are more exp efficient at stealth or uncovering secrets than Demons then either Princesses are over powered or Demons are underpowered and either way something needs fixing.<br /> <br /> Perhaps niche protection is a better word than balance. If the thematics say Werewolves should be better fighters than Princesses and Princesses should be better social characters than Werewolves (both true) I'd want the mechanics to reflect that.<br /> <br /> This is getting way of topic though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:45:37-07:00","id":583775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583744#post583744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes get the insanity vibe; but I agreed with the general thrust of the criticisms anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good for you. I won't put an account on there unless employers demand me to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um. You talking about Beast or Vampire here? </div> </div> </div>Originally, Vampire, which you think would be obvious from the context clues.<br /> <br /> Now? Both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:56:58-07:00","id":583780,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah was the table and formula for how much satiety a Beast could potentially gain from a feeding in the old draft?<br /> <br /> By the way it looks like they pulled &quot;You are Meat&quot; from the nightmare list. It still shows up in other parts of the document like on other Beast's stat blocks and the tip for creating Nightmares that don't kill the target, but the actual Nightmare is not listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  added an observation and question 07-08-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:02:44-07:00","id":583785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583780#post583780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah was the table and formula for how much satiety a Beast could potentially gain from a feeding in the old draft?</div> </div> </div> </div>The table was for determining how many dice you started with before the modifiers; you only rolled if the total was equal to or higher than your current Satiety, and unless you rolled an exceptional success you always gained a dot of Satiety per success (exceptional success allowed you to hold off at Satiety 9 if the result would normally bring you to 10).<br /> <br /> Apart from the modifier table shifting around a fair amount (most notably the change to how much killing in the process is worth), this is the same now as it was in the first draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:09:37-07:00","id":583789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583785#post583785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The table was for determining how many dice you started with before the modifiers; you only rolled if the total was equal to or higher than your current Satiety, and unless you rolled an exceptional success you always gained a dot of Satiety per success (exceptional success allowed you to hold off at Satiety 9 if the result would normally bring you to 10).<br /> <br /> Apart from the modifier table shifting around a fair amount (most notably the change to how much killing in the process is worth), this is the same now as it was in the first draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright thanks. Wasn't sure and didn't want to scrounge through the old document for a table I wasn't sure existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:45:44-07:00","id":584838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583698#post583698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rpg.net is <i>batshit insane</i>.<br /> <br /> We should be fine here. I think. Maybe.<br /> <br /> It doesn't change the fact that there's a lot of obvious allegory going on, although a large part of the is the fault of popular vampire media and Stoker's hangups.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anne Rice didn't do the genre any particular favors (so much pedephelia...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:02:27-07:00","id":584853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=584838#post584838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anne Rice didn't do the genre any particular favors (so much pedephelia...).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She's a horror writer who knowingly presented things that are horrific as horrific. She isn't Stephanie Meyers presenting twisted abusive relationships as moral. As for the favors she did the genre, she's the entire reason we have &quot;horror of BEING a vampire&quot; as a narrative concept. The World of Darkness would literally not exist without her work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:11:23-07:00","id":584856,"title":"","content":"My point is that, yes, pop-culture vampires are tied to their use as a vehicle for rape messages, by a lot. Requiem has gotten mileage by playing around with the icons with the knowledge of the common meaning in the back of their mind. And yes, that is a measuring stick for how we can look at and regard Beast. RPG.net having a shitfest over it doesn't change this broad context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:23:27-07:00","id":585022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=584853#post584853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a horror writer who knowingly presented things that are horrific as horrific. She isn't Stephanie Meyers presenting twisted abusive relationships as moral. As for the favors she did the genre, she's the entire reason we have &quot;horror of BEING a vampire&quot; as a narrative concept. The World of Darkness would literally not exist without her work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you may like her works, I'll stick with Stoker. I do think it's more than a little strong to say that the World of Darkness would not exist without her work. Certainly her works, along with many others have influenced WoDs development and evolution but IMO World of Darkness was an inevitable outgrowth of the way the RPG industry was growing in the 80s. If White Wolf hadn't been founded around it, we would certainly still have it in another form. The horror genre itself is one of the better defined ones and certainly has a long lineage and it's only natural to have RPGs focused on it much as we did (and still do) for fantasy, pulp, superheroes, cyberpunk, and science fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:33:54-07:00","id":585032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=584856#post584856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that, yes, pop-culture vampires are tied to their use as a vehicle for rape messages, by a lot. Requiem has gotten mileage by playing around with the icons with the knowledge of the common meaning in the back of their mind. And yes, that is a measuring stick for how we can look at and regard Beast. RPG.net having a shitfest over it doesn't change this broad context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rape isn't the kind of thing that I've associated with Vampire as much as Changeling. But I sense there may be a generation gap here. Certainly Marvel characters like the Purple Man and Starfox did not seem that rapey by the standards of the 60s and 70s. The same is not true today, you can't have a superhero whose superpower is simply pheromones that make women do anything you want. The times are changing and how games are written has to be sensitive to that or you'll end up with mega-alienation. Note I'm not saying that the umbrage on RPG.net is right but it isn't all wrong either.<br /> <br /> I still personally think that it reflects more character agency if the Horror doing the Devouring is the Beast's own subconscious self rather than Joe Beast down the block but YMMV. It's a simple enough fluff tweak for me and my players to agree to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:46:50-07:00","id":585044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=583780#post583780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way it looks like they pulled &amp;quot;You are Meat&amp;quot; from the nightmare list. It still shows up in other parts of the document like on other Beast's stat blocks and the tip for creating Nightmares that don't kill the target, but the actual Nightmare is not listed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Does it make me a bad person that this makes me feel kind of sad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:21:09-07:00","id":585067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=585032#post585032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rape isn't the kind of thing that I've associated with Vampire as much as Changeling. But I sense there may be a generation gap here. Certainly Marvel characters like the Purple Man and Starfox did not seem that rapey by the standards of the 60s and 70s. The same is not true today, you can't have a superhero whose superpower is simply pheromones that make women do anything you want. The times are changing and how games are written has to be sensitive to that or you'll end up with mega-alienation. Note I'm not saying that the umbrage on RPG.net is right but it isn't all wrong either.<br /> <br /> I still personally think that it reflects more character agency if the Horror doing the Devouring is the Beast's own subconscious self rather than Joe Beast down the block but YMMV. It's a simple enough fluff tweak for me and my players to agree to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rape <i>can</i> be Changeling, don't get me wrong. That said, a popular read of the original Dracula tackles it as Stoker struggling with a lot of his own ideas with sex and sexuality, and that style of reading becomes more prominent when you mix in the stuff of Anne Rice. There's a rich thread of &quot;fear of sex/uality&quot; expressed in a lot of pop media in vampires, with sex being used aggressively, to attack, to dominate, etc., etc. Requiem is more a game about addiction than anything else, but because sense and sensuality are big elements of addiction and there is the cultural background of dangerous sex to vampires, Requiem has a lot of ways it exists as a metaphor for rape and all the ugly subjects around it-namely in the way it explores a need for intimacy being exploited for other peoples needs. So basically, while Requiem is not about rape, it can't escape the easy metaphor of vampires as a collection of feelings about things that are involved with rape.<br /> <br /> Changeling <i>can</i> be about that, but it's less specifically about the manipulation of need against one another and more broadly about trauma of all sorts, an aspect being emphasized more in Second Edition. As an example, Lara Croft from the last Tomb Raider and Tom Hanks from Cast Away can apply as easily as Alice, Dorothy, and Wendy from Lost Girls can.<br /> <br /> As for Beast, I don't see much differentiation between the Horror being the subconscious and it's own thing. A Beast's Soul/Horror is a shard bridging the collective soul of humanity and the world itself, and that makes for some trippy interactions with the self. It leads to the same place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-09-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:15:25-07:00","id":585185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=585032#post585032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still personally think that it reflects more character agency if the Horror doing the Devouring is the Beast's own subconscious self rather than Joe Beast down the block but YMMV. It's a simple enough fluff tweak for me and my players to agree to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, it <i>can</i> in fact be like that? There isn't any need to tweak fluff to allow it. In the current version of the revisions, self-Devourings are presented as validly as those assisted by the Horror of another Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:17:14-07:00","id":586841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=585022#post585022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you may like her works, I'll stick with Stoker.</div> </div> </div> </div>False dichotomy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think it's more than a little strong to say that the World of Darkness would not exist without her work. </div> </div> </div>No it really isn't. Vampire the Masquerade is pretty much a straight up love letter Interview and its sequels. To the point of there being wide common accusations of it having been a rip-off. The device of the horror of the <i><b>VAMPIRE'S POV</b></i>, struggling to be human while having murderous needs (something Stoker did not do) is her primary contribution to the genre - or at very least the popularizer of it (if there was some lesser known predecessor whose work I'm not aware of).<br /> <br /> Not to mention in her later books in the series she had the ancient forbearer of vampiric kind, whose rising spelled doom for her descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:23:16-07:00","id":586843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=585044#post585044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Does it make me a bad person that this makes me feel kind of sad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, it was an interesting power and most certainly an excellent ace to keep up your sleeve. Of course those traces of it still in the book might also mean that they plan to put it back in once they've done some patching to deal with whatever problems caused them to remove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T04:16:55-07:00","id":586946,"title":"","content":"Can we keep this on topic, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:45:06-07:00","id":587114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=586843#post586843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, it was an interesting power and most certainly an excellent ace to keep up your sleeve. Of course those traces of it still in the book might also mean that they plan to put it back in once they've done some patching to deal with whatever problems caused them to remove it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a power I want to revisit at some point, but the whole notion of &quot;soul&quot; gets misinterpreted a lot in NWoD and needed more clarification than we had time to give it there, especially WRT other supernatural creatures. We'll probably include a similar Nightmare in a future book, and make sure we have time to discuss &quot;souls&quot; and what they are in context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:53:25-07:00","id":587700,"title":"","content":"Tinkering with it myself, I feel like it really should have different effects on supernaturals depending on the nature of and their relationship to their soul. Like suppressing a vampire's soul should result in Frenzy, given that it's the bulwark against the beast. Losing their soul completely results not in a Thrall, but Draugr.<br /> <br /> Similarly, supress the soul of a Sin-Eatter, and they have someone else waiting to take the wheel!<br /> <br /> The &quot;normal&quot; effects of You Are Meat (i.e. illusory soul-suppression), play out as with humans on Prometheans - but try to poke their actual soul with Satiety expenditure, and you'll unleash a Firestorm instead!<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't have human souls to suppress - they instead are half-spirit through their entire form. Poke that, and they'll reflexively shapeshift in self-defense (+ possible Death Rage). Nothing gets supressed.<br /> <br /> Suppress the soul of a Mummy, and their Memory melts away. They may be Thralled, but it won't be to the Beast. Instead they revert to &quot;Purpose-Drones&quot; ala their state when they first rise. It is the Judges who they revert to serve. Mummies who have achieved Apotheosis are immune to the Nightmare - they've fought too hard to win rulership of their own soul for any statable power to mess with it so easily.<br /> <br /> Just a few off hand thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:45:13-07:00","id":588045,"title":"","content":"With Vampires it depends whether you consider the beast part of a vampire's soul or just latched on it, so if it should end in a draugr seems debatable. And werewolves <i>do</i> have souls of a sort, since some Idigam have the ability to tear them out and replace them with spirits to create Empty Wolves. Other than that, sounds about right.<br /> <br /> I'm actually not sure about Mummies, since their sahu is literally held together by their deathless soul, animated by the Sekhem that flows through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T06:41:59-07:00","id":588099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=584856#post584856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Requiem has gotten mileage by playing around with the icons with the knowledge of the common meaning in the back of their mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Could you clarify what you mean by this? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:02:00-07:00","id":588145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=586841#post586841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it really isn't. Vampire the Masquerade is pretty much a straight up love letter Interview and its sequels. To the point of there being wide common accusations of it having been a rip-off. The device of the horror of the <i><b>VAMPIRE'S POV</b></i>, struggling to be human while having murderous needs (something Stoker did not do) is her primary contribution to the genre - or at very least the popularizer of it (if there was some lesser known predecessor whose work I'm not aware of).</div> </div> </div> </div>You said WoD not Vampire. A horror themed RPG emerging by the late 80s / early 90s was quite inevitable. Anne Rice was definitely an input into the shape of Vampire: the Masquerade however, both Rice and the game are also drawing on previous works such as <i>Barnaby Collins</i>, <i>Dark Shadows</i>, Stoker's <i>Dracula</i>, and <i>Carmilla</i> among others. Anne Rice is not the end all, be all of vampire literature let alone horror literature. WoD definitely doesn't owe the fact of its very existence to Anne Rice. Also vis-a-vis struggling with murderous needs, Dan Curtis's Dark Shadows beats her to the punch by almost a decade. I'm sure with a little more digging I can find additional examples. Like Tolkein, Rice is not a holy cow and WoD is not one of Rice's works. She merely serves as one among a very large number of inputs into its shape. That we have it at all though is a product of the late 80s RPG community's zeitgeist and not simply because someone licensed one author's works to make a game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:09:51-07:00","id":588632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=587114#post587114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's a power I want to revisit at some point, but the whole notion of &quot;soul&quot; gets misinterpreted a lot in NWoD and needed more clarification than we had time to give it there, especially WRT other supernatural creatures. We'll probably include a similar Nightmare in a future book, and make sure we have time to discuss &quot;souls&quot; and what they are in context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any chance of another new Nightmare stepping in for the core? Like one playing on dreams of being naked in public that strips away disguises, exposing someone's true face....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:42:52-07:00","id":588694,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Regarding the concern that Beast loses thematic perspective by giving focus to the Lessons that Beasts teach, I have to disagree. It is made clear in the Kickstarter that a Lesson is the IDEAL outcome of the victim making through the fear, not the <i>raison d' \u00eatre </i>of the Begotten. Furthermore, it is also stated that in the distant, mythical past, the <i>Heroes </i>were the ones who taught the Lessons after confronting the Beast and surviving. Unfortunately, the explosive growth of the human population/tools and the increasing sense of having nothing to truly fear caused a shift in the monster slaying narrative. Heroes don't want to be actually heroic, they just want to be admired and praised for looking like they are, the price be damned. The Beasts now fill the narrative vacuum left by Heroes, leading to an inversion of roles. That is the crux of this game: an ancient story re-imagined to show the viewpoint of someone that used to have no purpose beyond being defeated to further someone else's story. Asking Beasts to boil down to sneering, remorseless things reduces them to the unfair caricatures that Heroes perceive and want to <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>burn. </b></span><br /> <br /> In short, it defeats the purpose of the game. Going down that road beats the purpose of playing the monster in the World Of Darkness. If you want to play as a thing to be only feared instead of feared and revered, I suggest you look for another game.<br /> <br /> I sincerely apologize if this post comes across as rude or confrontational. I am just sharing my heartfelt opinion in a way I believe is clear and incisive. I am not better than you for role playing like this or that. Do what you find the most fun, but be mindful of where you can get the most of this fun you are searching for.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-12-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:25:40-07:00","id":588730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=588632#post588632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Any chance of another new Nightmare stepping in for the core? Like one playing on dreams of being naked in public that strips away disguises, exposing someone's true face....</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the nightmare archetype the Ugallu are based off of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:11:57-07:00","id":588771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=588730#post588730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that the nightmare archetype the Ugallu are based off of?</div> </div> </div> </div>It overlaps with their concept. As far as I'm aware there's no power that specifically plays on that fear/nightmare (a visibility to everyone, not just a specific predator is part of it).<br /> <br /> It's not like other nightmares don't overlap with fear of hopelessness/weakness, fear of revulsion, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T03:38:14-07:00","id":588994,"title":"","content":"I'm Curious... Haven't Read the Full document (I prefer too have a actual Book rather then a document) Have they ever said that Beasts Can't feed on other Supernaturals? Just thinking if you could get a &quot;Super-Predator&quot; or Apex that feeds on the Fear of other Supernaturals... Maybe only one Type though. (Mostly thinking this because of something from one of the Legends/Mythology Books from Vampire.. About a &quot;Entity&quot; that Feed on Entire Cities of Vampires, causing Paranoia and fear amongst them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:29:56-07:00","id":589169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=588994#post588994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Curious... Haven't Read the Full document (I prefer too have a actual Book rather then a document) Have they ever said that Beasts Can't feed on other Supernaturals? Just thinking if you could get a &quot;Super-Predator&quot; or Apex that feeds on the Fear of other Supernaturals... Maybe only one Type though. (Mostly thinking this because of something from one of the Legends/Mythology Books from Vampire.. About a &quot;Entity&quot; that Feed on Entire Cities of Vampires, causing Paranoia and fear amongst them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that they could. It's another slight issue with the cross-over bits vs existing Beast fluff. If the goal of feeding is to teach lessons (i.e., Wisdom) wouldn't other supernaturals actually be the best targets of all? After all, don't they prey on humans, lord it over humans, etc.? Hopefully these kinds of things will be addressed in future drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:04:23-07:00","id":589208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=589169#post589169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume that they could. It's another slight issue with the cross-over bits vs existing Beast fluff. If the goal of feeding is to teach lessons (i.e., Wisdom) wouldn't other supernaturals actually be the best targets of all? After all, don't they prey on humans, lord it over humans, etc.? Hopefully these kinds of things will be addressed in future drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Could see a &quot;Sub-Faction&quot; of Begotten who take it as their duty to educate The other Splats at both the Pluses and Minuses of their condition.<br /> Also does mean they could be used as antagonists for the other lines just as easy as they can crossover with them. Maybe also have them as/with a Hunter conspiracy (With Reformed Heroes) as &quot;Terrors to show that there is always something more Dangerous in the Shadows&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:29:37-07:00","id":589239,"title":"","content":"It's not really the goal so much as a cultural meaning Beasts tend to attach to feeding their Hungers. The Horror doesn't care, even if that may have been the role of the Primordial Dream in the survival and evolution of mankind in ancient times.<br /> <br /> If the idea is actually true, then at the time it was likely just a natural cycle that had no need for the Begotten to interject as anything more than monsters according to their conscience. Of course, with Heroes apparently diverging from their original purpose and there just being so many people the Dream doesn't reach large numbers, things don't take care of themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:35:03-08:00","id":751893,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to understand the sidebar on page 99. When the Horror/Soul is alone in the Lair it can use any level of Atavisms. Normal, Low Satiety, and Satiety Expenditure are all available to it though it must still spend Satiety for the last part. When the Soul and the Beast join together physically, you only get Low Satiety if you're at Low Satiety. Why? I'm trying to understand what dulls the fangs/claws of your Soul or what weakens their armor. If you physically join together shouldn't you get the benefit of the Low Satiety anyways since it's physically present, I feel taking that away takes a bit of the bite out of &quot;Behold my True Form&quot; moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6403-ahzouroshadow","name":"ahzouroshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:56:46-08:00","id":751932,"title":"","content":"The idea is that part of the Horror's power comes from it's unreasoning nature. When a Beast merges with their Horror, they retain their intellect and intelligence (and ability to use Nightmares!), but lose some of that ravenous power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:31:42-08:00","id":752005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=588694#post588694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Regarding the concern that Beast loses thematic perspective by giving focus to the Lessons that Beasts teach, I have to disagree. It is made clear in the Kickstarter that a Lesson is the IDEAL outcome of the victim making through the fear, not the <i>raison d' \u00eatre </i>of the Begotten. Furthermore, it is also stated that in the distant, mythical past, the <i>Heroes </i>were the ones who taught the Lessons after confronting the Beast and surviving. Unfortunately, the explosive growth of the human population/tools and the increasing sense of having nothing to truly fear caused a shift in the monster slaying narrative. Heroes don't want to be actually heroic, they just want to be admired and praised for looking like they are, the price be damned. The Beasts now fill the narrative vacuum left by Heroes, leading to an inversion of roles. That is the crux of this game: an ancient story re-imagined to show the viewpoint of someone that used to have no purpose beyond being defeated to further someone else's story.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the case, then the Lessons need to be less obviously tacked on as an afterthought. And they are tacked on. They're a way to make the Beasts feel less horrible to the player (and possibly to themselves) by letting them try to justify themselves and what they do with the claim of teaching valuable Aesops, but it's a smoke screen. The Aesops are broken ones at best, and they aren't doing humanity any favors by teaching them; they're just feeding their own hunger. And Heroes aren't flawed because they no longer teach the Lessons; heroes are flawed because they imagine themselves to be the main characters in a story. They don't want to accept the fact that life isn't a story, and it doesn't have protagonists, and it may not mean anything at all. That it's just life. So rather than grapple with the idea of their own insignificance and of the challenges of finding meaning where there may or may not be any inherent meaning at all, they retreat into this fantasy land where they are the heroes triumphantly slaying monsters. Which probably makes them uncomfortably close to a 'Take That!' to the players of games that have as their premise that the player characters are the heroes of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T00:20:50-08:00","id":758135,"title":"","content":"I just pulled up the original Kickstarter draft, and noticed something odd. The original version is 457 pages long, with no backer names. But the beta release that we're proofreading is only 351 . . . with backer names. Is there a list somewhere of what was cut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T00:30:45-08:00","id":758142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes?p=758135#post758135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just pulled up the original Kickstarter draft, and noticed something odd. The original version is 457 pages long, with no backer names. But the beta release that we're proofreading is only 351 . . . with backer names. Is there a list somewhere of what was cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've discovered the magic of formatting.<br /> <br /> To give you a very brief and basic idea of what that statement means: the first draft's ToC is twelve pages long.<br /> <br /> The book draft's is five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}